# Database — SQLite Rules

## SQLite Configuration
On every app start, run these PRAGMAs before anything else:
```sql
PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;        -- enables concurrent reads
PRAGMA synchronous = NORMAL;      -- safe + fast (not OFF)
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;         -- enforce FK constraints
PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000;       -- wait up to 5s on lock
PRAGMA cache_size = -20000;       -- 20MB page cache
PRAGMA temp_store = MEMORY;       -- temp tables in RAM
```

## Connection Pool
```rust
let pool = sqlx::sqlite::SqlitePoolOptions::new()
    .max_connections(1)   // SQLite WAL supports 1 writer
    .min_connections(1)
    .connect(&database_url).await?;
```
**Important:** SQLite in WAL mode supports multiple concurrent readers but only one writer. Use a pool of 1 write connection. For read-heavy paths, open a separate read pool with max_connections(4).

## Migrations
- All migrations live in `backend/src/db/migrations/`
- Filename format: `0001_initial.sql`, `0002_add_labels.sql`
- Use `sqlx::migrate!()` macro to run on startup
- Migrations are **append-only** — never edit an existing migration file
- Never drop columns in SQLite (it doesn't support it) — add new columns only

## Schema Rules
- Primary keys: `TEXT` (UUID strings), never INTEGER autoincrement
- Timestamps: `INTEGER` (Unix milliseconds), never TEXT dates
- Booleans: `INTEGER` (0 or 1), never TEXT
- JSON payloads: `TEXT` (serialize to JSON string before storing)
- Positions: `REAL` (float for fractional indexing)

## Query Rules
- Always use `sqlx::query!` or `sqlx::query_as!` macros — never raw string queries
- Always add indexes for foreign keys and frequently filtered columns:
```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_cards_list_id ON cards(list_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_cards_board_id ON cards(board_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_activity_log_card_id ON activity_log(card_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_notifications_user_id ON notifications(user_id);
```
- For paginated queries, always use cursor-based pagination (by `created_at`), not OFFSET

## Soft Deletes
- Boards use `archived INTEGER DEFAULT 0` (not hard delete)
- Cards, lists, comments use hard delete — cascade via FK
- When a board is deleted: archive it, do not cascade delete cards (data safety)
- When a list is deleted: move its cards to a default "Archive" list or hard delete (ask user)

## Cascade Rules
Define in schema:
```sql
FOREIGN KEY (list_id) REFERENCES lists(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
```
Cards cascade delete when their list is deleted.
Assignees, labels, attachments, time_entries, comments cascade delete when their card is deleted.
Activity log entries are kept even if the card is deleted (set card_id to NULL).

## Backup
The binary must support a simple backup command:
```
zeroboard backup --output ./backup.db
```
This runs `VACUUM INTO 'backup.db'` — a safe online backup of SQLite.

## Never Do
- Never run raw user input in SQL
- Never store unhashed passwords
- Never store JWT secrets in the database
- Never use `SELECT *` — always name columns explicitly
- Never ignore sqlx errors — always propagate with `?`
